sparky-stereo-camera (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Save only what is a setting (ORDER 678): no inactive, read-only,
    write-only, volatile, relative or speed control, action or control
    without a range; every V4L2 control flag has its rule.
  * Apply governing controls before the values they govern, with fresh
    flags; a saved setting still inactive is not a failure.
  * Clean an entry written by 0.1.0 to 0.1.2 once, each removal logged,
    and clear the problems kept for those entries.
  * A camera nobody set starts at its largest picture and, at that size,
    its highest frame rate (ORDER 682); a known machine's caveat can name
    the formats to use. New command: best NAME.
  * Keep a refused mode or reset said on the page; translate five more
    packing names from the stereo layer's catalogues.
  * Know a camera plugged in again by PipeWire's object.serial: a node id
    is given again, so a quick replug was not applied.
  * An old store keeps the values of controls that are inactive now: they
    may be the person's own; they wait and are set when the control is
    active again, also when the person switches its governing control.
    Journal lines say only what is known.
  * A camera not found is said (exit 1) after asking PipeWire again for 3 s;
    a listed camera whose device does not answer is said, never answered
    with an empty list; the user service tries it again at its next pass.
  * The page says that Qt Multimedia and PipeWire programs follow the
    default camera and choose their own size and frame rate.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:59:00 +0000

